Non-ASCII °C in a bash fixture + Process.run output — encoding: Process.run decodes with systemEncoding (utf-8 on linux). Fine on the linux runner; on Windows would break but this repo's CI is linux (mac for some). Use plain "C" to be safe? The °C is narrative sugar; I'll keep the fixture pure ASCII ("30.3C") to stay hermetic — actually let me keep it simple ASCII to avoid any locale questions (the ticket even mentions locale/encoding-dependent output as a divergence axis, but for a hermetic test ASCII is safer).

